    "collective_statement_most_likely_to_succeed": "Candidate 1 is the most likely to succeed because it perfectly executes the mandatory ATS directives while demonstrating exceptional statutory precision. It correctly identifies the recent statutory 60% fee reduction for Small Entities under the Unleashing American Innovators Act of 2022, which validates the fee calculations. It preemptively cures formalities by filing a Substitute Specification to excise embedded drawings, claims, and abstracts, and strategically deletes the 'Statement of License Grant' to preserve the Small Entity status. Furthermore, it flawlessly executes the required subset-sum knapsack fee allocation strategy under 37 CFR 1.22(b), directing the exact $416.00 in unapplied credits to the Basic Filing Fee ($70) and Search Fee ($308), minimizing stranded funds. The assertive and clear language ensures the Office of Petitions and the pre-examination clerks have no ambiguity regarding the superseding nature of this response.",
    "unlikely_to_succeed_reasons": null,
    "ats_alignment_assessment": "The candidate aligns perfectly with the ATS brief. It addresses the imminent 3-month extension deadline, applies the unapplied credits exactly as mathematically optimized by the knapsack analysis, remits the remaining fresh funds, and preemptively cures the specification formalities.",
